  "items": [
    {
      "_id": "9CIXNyHa6hxMxmO2",
      "name": "Crush",
      "type": "weapon",
      "system": {
        "source": {
          "custom": "",
          "book": "MM'14",
          "page": "46",
          "license": "",
          "rules": "2014",
          "revision": 1
        },
        "description": {
          "value": "<div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><i>Melee Weapon Attack:</i> [[/r 1d20+5]]{+5} to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. <i>Hit:</i> 6 ([[/damage 1d6 + 3 type=bludgeoning]]) damage, and the darkmantle attaches to the target. If the target is Medium or smaller and the darkmantle has advantage on the attack roll, it attaches by engulfing the target's head, and the target is also &amp;Reference[condition=blinded] and unable to breathe while the darkmantle is attached in this way.</p><p>While attached to the target, the darkmantle can attack no other creature except the target but has advantage on its attack rolls. The darkmantle's speed also becomes 0, it can't benefit from any bonus to its speed, and it moves with the target.</p><p>A creature can detach the darkmantle by making a successful [[/save ability=str dc=13]] check as an action. On its turn, the darkmantle can detach itself from the target by using 5 feet of movement.</p></div>",
